ting\":\"PG\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"a54yC1etmVc\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2003-10-09\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-12-13\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":7.924,\"tmdbId\":\"10719\",\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"18407\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"Elf (2D) [PG]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"419\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"364658\",\"time\":\"2025-11-06T17:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":6,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":95,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser christmas\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"362864\",\"time\":\"2025-12-13T10:30:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":0,\"screenId\":\"442\",\"seatsRemaining\":60,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser kids-club christmas\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"362865\",\"time\":\"2025-12-24T15:30:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":18,\"screenId\":\"442\",\"seatsRemaining\":42,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser christmas\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"362866\",\"time\":\"2025-12-26T13:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":0,\"screenId\":\"442\",\"seatsRemaining\":60,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser christmas\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"29178\",\"name\":\"National Theatre Live: Hamlet\",\"showingStatus\":\"Has Played\",\"urlSlug\":\"national-theatre-live-hamlet\",\"posterImage\":\"oqp5egh0yzd8ybmg7kjydk54kgw1\",\"bannerImage\":\"ikbozckm4jx0qxj7pdoh46fg7j06\",\"synopsis\":\"Olivier Award-winner Hiran Abeysekera (Life of Pi) is Hamlet in this fearless, contemporary take on Shakespeare’s famous tragedy.\\n \\nTrapped between duty and doubt, surrounded by power and privilege, young Prince Hamlet dares to ask the ultimate question – you know the one.\\n \\nNational Theatre Deputy Artistic Director, Robert Hastie (Standing at the Sky’s Edge, Operation Mincemeat) directs this sharp, stylish and darkly funny reimagining.\",\"starring\":\"Hiran Abeysekera\",\"directedBy\":\"Robert Hastie\",\"producedBy\":null,\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":180,\"genre\":null,\"allGenres\":null,\"rating\":\"TBC\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"d6omHChNvlw\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2026-01-22\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2026-01-22\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"475714\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"Lrc Hamlet - NT Live 2026 (Theatre) [Unknown]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"411\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"364657\",\"time\":\"2025-11-06T19:30:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":1,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":100,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"362957\",\"time\":\"2026-01-22T19:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":17,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":84,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"362958\",\"time\":\"2026-02-02T13:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":1,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":100,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"362959\",\"time\":\"2026-02-18T19:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":0,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":101,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"29176\",\"name\":\"The Metropolitan Opera: La Bohème\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"the-metropolitan-opera-la-bohme\",\"posterImage\":\"bg8vrw0us2ro66st6vhmb9h3cgt8\",\"bannerImage\":\"65bwe18dtu4ikjtr0olv1woz1ly9\",\"synopsis\":\"With its enchanting setting and spellbinding score, the world’s most popular opera is as timeless as it is heartbreaking.\\nFranco Zeffirelli’s picture-perfect production brings 19th-century Paris to the Met stage as Puccini’s young friends and lovers navigate the joy and struggle of bohemian life. Soprano Juliana Grigoryan is the feeble seamstress Mimì, opposite tenor Freddie De Tommaso as the ardent poet Rodolfo.\\nKeri-Lynn Wilson conducts the November 8 performance, which will be transmitted live from the Met stage to cinemas worldwide.\",\"starring\":\"Evgeny Nikitin, Franz-Josef Selig, David Portillo\",\"directedBy\":\"Gary Halvorson, François Girard\",\"producedBy\":\"\",\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":165,\"genre\":\"Music\",\"allGenres\":\"Music\",\"rating\":\"12A\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"lU0w-kpa_Wo\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-11-08\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-11-08\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":1.7745,\"tmdbId\":\"616155\",\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"465756\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"LA BOHEMEÂ - MET OPERA 2025 (OPERA) [Unknown]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"411\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"360663\",\"time\":\"2025-11-08T18:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":54,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":48,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"360678\",\"time\":\"2025-11-11T13:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":19,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":82,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"31311\",\"name\":\"A Minecraft Movie\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"a-minecraft-movie\",\"posterImage\":\"xf07ekuxiyifc4g6e0wkgc7xxrsd\",\"bannerImage\":\"d6qimpiovvgl4wgoc9yd988olpu6\",\"synopsis\":\"Welcome to the world of Minecraft, where creativity doesn’t just help you craft, it’s essential to one’s survival!  Four misfits—Garrett “The Garbage Man” Garrison (Momoa), Henry (Hansen), Natalie (Myers) and Dawn (Brooks)—find themselves struggling with ordinary problems when they are suddenly pulled through a mysterious portal into the Overworld: a bizarre, cubic wonderland that thrives on imagination.  To get back home, they’ll have to master this world (and protect it from evil things like Piglins and Zombies, too) while embarking on a magical quest with an unexpected, expert crafter, Steve (Black).  Together, their adventure will challenge all five to be bold and to reconnect with the qualities that make each of them uniquely creative…the very skills they need to thrive back in the real world.\",\"starring\":\"Jason Momoa, Jack Black, Sebastian Eugene Hansen\",\"directedBy\":\"Jared Hess\",\"producedBy\":\"Jason Momoa, Roy Lee, Cale Boyter, Mary Parent, Jon Berg, Vu Bui, Jill Messick, Torfi Frans Ólafsson\",\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":101,\"genre\":\"Adventure\",\"allGenres\":\"Adventure, Fantasy, Family, Action\",\"rating\":\"PG\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"iLO4oQwn80g\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-04-04\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-11-08\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":25.8837,\"tmdbId\":\"950387\",\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"169976\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"MINECRAFT MOVIE, A [PG]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"410\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"364478\",\"time\":\"2025-11-08T10:30:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":4,\"screenId\":\"442\",\"seatsRemaining\":56,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser kids-club\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"364479\",\"time\":\"2025-11-09T10:30:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":0,\"screenId\":\"442\",\"seatsRemaining\":60,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser kids-club\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"31552\",\"name\":\"Gabby's Dollhouse: The Movie\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"gabbys-dollhouse-the-movie\",\"posterImage\":\"a7uslllnbo1oynvxc0osmnn6m26e\",\"bannerImage\":\"ibskaz7ak7p4d4rns8yu8gtdtwuj\",\"synopsis\":\"In the new film, Gabby (Laila Lockhart Kraner, reprising her role from the series) heads out on a road trip with her Grandma Gigi (four-time Grammy Award winner Gloria Estefan) to the urban wonderland of Cat Francisco. But when Gabby’s dollhouse, her most prized possession, ends up in the hands of an eccentric cat lady named Vera (Oscar® nominee Kristen Wiig), Gabby sets off on an adventure through the real world to get the Gabby Cats back together and save the dollhouse before it’s too late.\",\"starring\":\"Laila Lockhart Kraner, Gloria Estefan, Kristen Wiig\",\"directedBy\":\"Ryan Crego\",\"producedBy\":\"Steven Schweickart\",\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":98,\"genre\":\"Family\",\"allGenres\":\"Family, Comedy, Adventure, Animation\",\"rating\":\"U\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"zeZNF4pBXpI\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-10-17\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-11-08\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":29.1513,\"tmdbId\":\"1280282\",\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"388749\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"GABBY'S DOLLHOUSE: THE MOVIE [Unknown]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"410\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"367567\",\"time\":\"2025-11-08T11:40:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":0,\"screenId\":\"441\",\"seatsRemaining\":101,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"367564\",\"time\":\"2025-11-08T13:50:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":10,\"screenId\":\"442\",\"seatsRemaining\":50,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"367577\",\"time\":\"2025-11-09T11:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":0,\"screenId\":\"441\",\"seatsRemaining\":101,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"367578\",\"time\":\"2025-11-09T13:50:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":2,\"screenId\":\"441\",\"seatsRemaining\":99,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"29161\",\"name\":\"Exhibition On Screen: Caravaggio\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"exhibition-on-screen-caravaggio\",\"posterImage\":\"vif8f3djaj8eor4xpsv4p11lup2i\",\"bannerImage\":\"azf1ggkwm0fnyzhl9yim0k1mztwj\",\"synopsis\":\"Five years in production, this is the most extensive film ever made about one of the greatest artists of all time – Caravaggio.\\nFeaturing masterpiece after masterpiece and with first-hand testimony from the artist himself on the eve of his mysterious death, this beautiful new film reveals Caravaggio as never before.\\nMulti-award-winning film makers Phil Grabsky and David Bickerstaff delve into the hidden narratives of Caravaggio’s life, piecing together clues embedded\\nwithin his incredible art.\\nThe intriguing self- depictions within his works – sometimes disguised, sometimes in plain sight – offer a rare window into his psyche and personal struggles.\\nCaravaggio’s masterpieces are some of art’s most instantly recognisable. No one else uses his signature blend of dramatic light, intense naturalism and bold, striking figures. His incredible paintings have captivated audiences for centuries. But there lies a deeper mystery – one that still beckons us to\\nexplore. What do these masterpieces reveal about the man behind the brush? Join us as we explore the many clues that help us to finally understand the life\\n– and death – of this remarkable man.\",\"starring\":null,\"directedBy\":\"Phil Grabsky, David Bickerstaff\",\"producedBy\":null,\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":101,\"genre\":null,\"allGenres\":null,\"rating\":\"12A\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"P4bzA9uNXEU\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-11-11\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-11-11\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"470743\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"EXHIBITION ON SCREEN: CARAVAGGIO 2025 (EXHIBITION) [Unknown]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"411\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"360677\",\"time\":\"2025-11-11T18:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":53,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":48,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"362930\",\"time\":\"2025-11-18T14:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":44,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":57,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"31228\",\"name\":\"The Big Heat\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"the-big-heat\",\"posterImage\":\"ww6pvofibyiqee91jbqgizcla8ar\",\"bannerImage\":\"nrlz3sjj5vxwf0n5p15thi5a1ydd\",\"synopsis\":\"About the film:\\n“Violence is a frequent characteristic of noir crime thrillers, and that’s certainly true of Fritz Lang’s The Big Heat, which contains one of the most famously shocking moments in all of noir. Glenn Ford stars as dogged cop Dave Bannion, who goes up against a crime syndicate controlled by Mike Lagana (Alexander Scourby) and his vicious second-in-command Vince Stone (Lee Marvin). Gloria Grahame had one of her most iconic roles as Stone’s girlfriend Debby Marsh, who agrees to help Bannion.”\\n\\nAbout Noirvember:\\nLocal film critic and podcaster Matthew Turner returns for a second mini season of film noir classics, which will run exclusively at Chiswick Cinema throughout November 2025.\\n\\nBroadly speaking, the term film noir (coined by French film critics) refers to Hollywood thrillers and dramas from the 1940s and ’50s that were perceived to have a degree of darkness and cynicism, reflecting post-WII attitudes at the time. Film noir stories frequently revolve around crime, corruption, greed, illicit sex and murder, exposing the dark heart beating beneath the American Dream.\\n\\nJoin us for five film noir classics, all of which showcase key elements of the genre, from hard-boiled dialogue (derived from the detective novels that were often adapted into thrillers), voiceover narration and shadowy lighting to femme fatales, murder plots and decidely unhappy endings.\\n\\nLike last year, each film will be introduced by Matthew Turner, a lifelong film noir enthusiast, who will also be around in the bar after each screening. In addition, audiences are invited to post about the films online, using the hashtag #Noirvember, a great source of other film noir recommendations.\",\"starring\":\"Jocelyn Brando, Lee Marvin, Glenn Ford, Gloria Grahame\",\"directedBy\":\"Fritz Lang\",\"producedBy\":null,\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":87,\"genre\":\"Thriller\",\"allGenres\":null,\"rating\":\"15\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ze6S3zZdSlA\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-11-12\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-11-12\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"999915\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"The Big Heat (2D) [15]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"419\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"363030\",\"time\":\"2025-11-12T19:45:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":22,\"screenId\":\"441\",\"seatsRemaining\":79,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser intro\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"29170\",\"name\":\"The Royal Ballet: La Fille Mal Gardée\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"the-royal-ballet-la-fille-mal-garde\",\"posterImage\":\"heaj9q6hez9ty6k9q29pgjmm6ji7\",\"bannerImage\":\"6xgkqg4ct2t6brv9915k8xy9mpxt\",\"synopsis\":\"Lise, the only daughter of Widow Simone, is in love with the young farmer Colas, but her mother has far more ambitious plans for her.\\nSimone hopes to marry her off to Alain, the son of the wealthy proprietor Thomas. Desperate to marry Colas rather than Alain, Lise contrives to outwit her mother’s plans.\\n65 years after its premiere, The Royal Ballet presents Frederick Ashton’s La Fille mal gardée. This affectionate portrayal of village life combines exuberant good humour and brilliantly inventive choreography in what is undoubtedly Ashton’s love letter to the English countryside. La Fille mal gardée whisks us away into pastoral bliss with Ferdinand Hérold’s cheerful score and Osbert Lancaster’s colourful designs.\\n\\nRuntime TBC\",\"starring\":\"James Hay, Francesca Hayward, Marcelino Sambé, Christopher Saunders, Joshua Junker\",\"directedBy\":\"Ross MacGibbon\",\"producedBy\":null,\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":210,\"genre\":null,\"allGenres\":null,\"rating\":\"12A\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"RkU1YDWYzQc\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-11-05\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-11-12\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"466183\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"LA FILLE MAL GARDEE - ROH, LONDON 2025 (BALLET) [Unknown]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"411\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"360683\",\"time\":\"2025-11-12T13:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":37,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":64,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"31159\",\"name\":\"Woman Grows Jeans\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"woman-grows-jeans\",\"posterImage\":\"sf3haqcretpgmj23dzbo213yhh92\",\"bannerImage\":\"d0hjldjab2nktg4ftxhxkky0n873\",\"synopsis\":\"When an ambitious experiment between a textile activist and a celebrity clothier meets inevitable challenges, one woman is propelled into an initiation that makes British fashion history. With a community of volunteers, they envisioned homegrown jeans sold through a social enterprise, but their work exposed uncomfortable truths about the systems controlling industry. Despite its sophistication, the U.K. can no longer produce clothing without importing materials or causing harm.\\n\\nIn a country buying 70 million pairs a year, Woman Grows Jeans journeys into our resilient ancestry to reclaim the care and agency that’s key to regeneration. After 600 hours, the UK’s only pair of homegrown jeans were handmade – not as a relic, but as a provocative signpost toward the future our hearts know is possible. A celebration of the traditional skills that reconnect us to nature’s wisdom, this documentary proves that the power to create change is still in our hands.\\n\\nJustine Aldersey-Williams is Director of natural dye studio The Wild Dyery, Co-Director of Homegrown Colour Ltd. and Founder of the Northern England Fibreshed – an international collective of textile professionals advocating for the use of bioregional and agroecologically grown fibres and dyes. She is an MA textiles/fashion graduate and a qualified educator specialising in botanical textile dyeing since 2011. She administrates a natural dye research community with over 13K members, has developed a comprehensive training which has reached thousands of students in 30+ countries and is a sought-after guest [lecturer and]speaker at industry events.\\n\\nJustine initiated the ‘Homegrown Homespun’ flax and indigo growing project in collaboration with fashion designer and TV judge on BBC 1’s Great British Sewing Bee, Patrick Grant and Lancashire-based cultural development programme The Super Slow Way. Aiming to grow jeans in the heartland of the British textile industry, her focus since 2020 has been experimenting with the upscaling of botanical indigo and linen production to a commercial scale. As a result of this Fibreshed collaboration, she recently made fashion history by growing her own pair of indigo linen jeans and has been featured in both national and regional press, including the ‘Field to Fashion’ episode of Countryfile, BBC Radio 5 Live Drive, Radio 4’s Open Country as well as numerous broadsheets, podcasts and magazines.\\n\\nJustine’s heritage skills and large following within the natural dye and fashion/textile communities have helped raise awareness of the need for a transition towards regenerative clothing, and her passionate activism is incentivising synthetic dye factories to consider renewable alternatives, by creating routes to market for plant dyes. Her documentary, ‘Woman Grows Jeans’ tells the pioneering story of the first pair of jeans to be grown on British soil and has been selected by the U.K. Green Film Network for screening across its independent cinemas nationwide.\",\"starring\":null,\"directedBy\":\"Justine Aldersley-Williams\",\"producedBy\":null,\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":50,\"genre\":\"Documentary\",\"allGenres\":null,\"rating\":\"18\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GIBk2k0Geek\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-11-13\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-11-13\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"8890253\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"Woman Grows Jeans (2D) [15]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"410\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"362730\",\"time\":\"2025-11-13T20:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":2,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":99,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser knitflicks\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"29181\",\"name\":\"John Cleese Packs It In\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"john-cleese-packs-it-in\",\"posterImage\":\"mvhdk0ly7543fmiawebdo9t6g0kj\",\"bannerImage\":\"svwxkume8dz4pr2wofdpmyh54iq5\",\"synopsis\":\"One of the most recognisable figures in British comedy, John Cleese’s career spans six decades - from his early days with the Cambridge Footlights to co-founding Monty Python, co-creating Fawlty Towers, and writing and starring in the Oscar-nominated “A Fish Called Wanda”. His unique brand of black humour has made him a global icon and intergalactic treasure.\\n\\nAt the age of eighty five, John Cleese sets off on what might be his final European tour - five countries, sixteen cities, twenty-three shows, and retaining just two original body parts. “John Cleese Packs It In” is a wry, behind-the-scenes portrait of a comedy legend on the road, battling various ailments, chaotic travel, and his own stubborn refusal to stop.\\n\\nSpanning six weeks on the road, the film captures Cleese unfiltered and on the move - riffing on life, fame, and the absurdity of getting old in front of thousands of fans. As he reflects on a stage career that began in 1963, the question lingers: is this the end of the road?\\n\\nWith unique and intimate access and showing unexpected tenderness, this is a documentary about legacy, laughter, and the dignity of bowing out… however reluctantly.\",\"starring\":\"John Cleese\",\"directedBy\":\"Andy Curd\",\"producedBy\":\"\",\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":80,\"genre\":\"Documentary\",\"allGenres\":\"Documentary\",\"rating\":\"12A\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"ZlBB4PUDEc8\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-11-13\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-11-13\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":0.2152,\"tmdbId\":\"1509739\",\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"476147\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"Lrc John Cleese Packs It In [Unknown]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"411\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"362821\",\"time\":\"2025-11-13T20:30:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":10,\"screenId\":\"442\",\"seatsRemaining\":50,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"31158\",\"name\":\"Four Lions\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"four-lions\",\"posterImage\":\"shqr6gt4bq60f9ucqiyi4cp9xoxp\",\"bannerImage\":\"ltk3ne3abvgzwnts05jl7fn0cfgt\",\"synopsis\":\"Nigel Lindsay talks to Jonathan Maitland about Four Lions.\\n\\nAbout the guests:\\nNigel Lindsay is one of the most experienced stage actors working in the UK today, collaborating with playwrights such as Harold Pinter and Tom Stoppard in more than forty plays in London.\\n\\nHe is known to many from his television role as Sir Robert Peel in the first two seasons of TV series Victoria, but in 2010 he played the opposite of a pillar of the establishment in the role of Barry, a Muslim convert in Chris Morris’s black comedy Four Lions, which follows a group of dim-witted homegrown jihadis planning a terrorist attack in Britain.\\n\\nThe film won a BAFTA and Nigel was nominated for Best British Comedy Performance at the British Film Awards for the role. 15 years on it is every bit as relevant. He talks to fellow Chiswickian, journalist, author and playwright Jonathan Maitland about it.\\n\\nJonathan was one of the financial backers of the film and he had a small part in it himself.\\n\\nChiswick in Film Festival 2025 is kindly sponsored by The London Bath Co. – superior, fully fitted bathrooms and kitchens – from design to installation.\\n\\nAbout CIFF:\\nThe festival is presented in close partnership between The Chiswick Calendar and The Chiswick Cinema.\\n\\nThe festival team are The Chiswick Calendar’s Editor Bridget Osborne, director and screenwriter Rob Sprackling, BAFTA-winning editor Andrea Carnevali and the cinema’s Programme and Marketing Manager Chris Parker.\\n\\nAbout the film:\\nFour incompetent British terrorists set out to train for and commit an act of terror.\",\"starring\":\"Riz Ahmed, Benedict Cumberbatch, Adeel Akhtar, Nigel Lindsay, Julia Davis,  Kayvan Novak, Arsher Ali, Craig Parkinson, Preeya Kalidas, Wasim Zakir\",\"directedBy\":\"Chris Morris\",\"producedBy\":null,\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":99,\"genre\":\"Comedy\",\"allGenres\":null,\"rating\":\"15\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ew-SrlQ9tlI\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-11-15\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-11-15\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"38999\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"Four Lions (2D) [15]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"420\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"362727\",\"time\":\"2025-11-15T20:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":37,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":64,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 laser qa ciff\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"31312\",\"name\":\"How to Train Your Dragon\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"how-to-train-your-dragon\",\"posterImage\":\"byurlxcsk61zamjrqy0ayvohfbwb\",\"bannerImage\":\"j35ha8xynw7rq037q39zzddr1wv4\",\"synopsis\":\"From three-time Oscar® nominee and Golden Globe winner Dean DeBlois, the creative visionary behind DreamWorks Animation’s acclaimed How to Train Your Dragon trilogy, comes a stunning live-action reimagining of the film that launched the beloved franchise. \\n\\nOn the rugged isle of Berk, where Vikings and dragons have been bitter enemies for generations, Hiccup (Mason Thames; The Black Phone, For All Mankind) stands apart. The inventive yet overlooked son of Chief Stoick the Vast (Gerard Butler, reprising his voice role from the animated franchise), Hiccup defies centuries of tradition when he befriends Toothless, a feared Night Fury dragon. Their unlikely bond reveals the true nature of dragons, challenging the very foundations of Viking society. \\n\\nWith the fierce and ambitious Astrid (BAFTA nominee Nico Parker; Dumbo, The Last of Us) and the village’s quirky blacksmith Gobber (Nick Frost; Snow White and the Huntsman, Shaun of the Dead) by his side, Hiccup confronts a world torn by fear and misunderstanding. \\n\\nAs an ancient threat emerges, endangering both Vikings and dragons, Hiccup’s friendship with Toothless becomes the key to forging a new future. Together, they must navigate the delicate path toward peace, soaring beyond the boundaries of their worlds and redefining what it means to be a hero and a leader.\",\"starring\":\"Mason Thames, Nico Parker, Gerard Butler\",\"directedBy\":\"Dean DeBlois\",\"producedBy\":\"Adam Siegel, Dean DeBlois, Marc Platt\",\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":126,\"genre\":\"Fantasy\",\"allGenres\":\"Fantasy, Adventure, Family\",\"rating\":\"PG\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"6DTDYRQZDmc\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-06-13\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-11-15\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":48.2321,\"tmdbId\":\"1087192\",\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"383400\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"How To Train Your Dragon (2D) [Unknown]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"410\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"364480\",\"time\":\"2025-11-15T10:30:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":0,\"screenId\":\"442\",\"seatsRemaining\":60,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser kids-club\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"364481\",\"time\":\"2025-11-16T10:30:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":0,\"screenId\":\"442\",\"seatsRemaining\":60,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser kids-club\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"31229\",\"name\":\"L'Atalante\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"latalante\",\"posterImage\":\"5hscoxoemlbgdnihrbz8lqrdltqz\",\"bannerImage\":\"ek4vr0pmkttec33v1e4nqcge5yas\",\"synopsis\":\"French Film expert Jon Davies hosts an informative and entertaining pre-film lecture before a hand-picked French film release in our new monthly club. The introduction lasts around sixty minutes, followed by a short break for refreshments followed by the film screening. French Impressions joins us from the Waterman’s Arts Centre, where Jon hosted it for over twenty years, with their kind consent.\\n\\nAbout the film:\\nNewly married couple Juliette and a ship captain Jean struggle through marriage as they travel on the L’atalante along with the captain’s first mate Le père Jules and a cabin boy.\",\"starring\":\"Michel Simon, Dita parlo, Jean Daste, Gilles Margaritis, Louis Lefebvre\",\"directedBy\":\"Jean Vigo\",\"producedBy\":null,\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":89,\"genre\":\"Thriller\",\"allGenres\":null,\"rating\":\"PG\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vzTN0YnKmOs\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-11-15\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-11-15\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"470058\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"L'ATALANTE (4K RE-ISSUE) [Unknown]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"419\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"363031\",\"time\":\"2025-11-15T11:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":13,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":88,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser intro french-impressions\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"31155\",\"name\":\"Ladies in Lavender\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"ladies-in-lavender\",\"posterImage\":\"1zs4ezej0cv7mcwxcukhxde7i87h\",\"bannerImage\":\"brln3826i6y8ghaloiileyaw6qac\",\"synopsis\":\"Charles Dance and Emma Hayter talk to Andrea Carnevali about Charles’ debut film.\\n\\nAbout the guests:\\nCharles Dance OBE is one of the UK’s best-known actors, capturing the market in steely-eyed, intimidating, authoritarian characters and villains (James Bond / For Your Eyes Only 1981, The Imitation Fame 2014, Game of Thrones, 2011 – 19).\\n\\nWith Ladies in Lavender he made his screen-writing and directorial debut, with two old friends, Dame Judi Dench and Dame Maggie Smith. \\n\\n“Beautiful setting, a succession of implausible incidents, and characteristically excellent work from Smith (all suppression and stoicism) and Dench (exuding unfulfilled yearning)” – Philip French in The Observer.\\n\\nEmma Hayter, who lives in Chiswick, has worked as a Producer, Executive Producer, Financier and Filmmaker on a number of feature films and television series, including Lovejoy and Taggart for television, Bafta-winning film My Summer of Love (2004) and Aisling Walsh’s directorial debut Joyriders (1988). Ladies in Lavender is a film of which she is “immensely proud”.\\n\\nChiswick in Film Festival 2025 is kindly sponsored by The London Bath Co. – superior, fully fitted bathrooms and kitchens – from design to installation.\\n\\nAbout CIFF:\\nThe festival is presented in close partnership between The Chiswick Calendar and The Chiswick Cinema.\\n\\nThe festival team are The Chiswick Calendar’s Editor Bridget Osborne, director and screenwriter Rob Sprackling, BAFTA-winning editor Andrea Carnevali and the cinema’s Programme and Marketing Manager Chris Parker.\\n\\nAbout the film:\\nAndrea, a gifted young Polish violinist from Krakow, is bound for America when he is swept overboard by a storm. When the Widdington sisters discover the handsome stranger on the beach below their house, they nurse him back to health. However, the presence of the musically talented young man disrupts the peaceful lives of Ursula and Janet and the community in which they live.\",\"starring\":\"Maggie Smith, Judi Dench, Daniel Bruhl, Freddie Jone, Natascha McElhone\",\"directedBy\":\"Charles Dance\",\"producedBy\":\"Emma Hayter\",\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":100,\"genre\":\"Drama\",\"allGenres\":null,\"rating\":\"18\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N8LKGIPn0FI\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-11-16\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-11-16\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"21208\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"Ladies In Lavender (2D) [12A]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"420\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"362726\",\"time\":\"2025-11-16T17:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":50,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":51,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"qa ciff\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"29159\",\"name\":\"National Theatre Live: The Fifth Step\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"national-theatre-live-the-fifth-step\",\"posterImage\":\"oz4w7ydtebonsoleei7io8iaizkz\",\"bannerImage\":\"wvd2vmy2so6auwou5fy2g905718k\",\"synopsis\":\"Olivier Award-winner Jack Lowden (Slow Horses, Dunkirk) is joined by Emmy and BAFTA-winner Martin Freeman (The Hobbit, The Responder) starring in the critically acclaimed and subversively funny new play by David Ireland. \\n \\nAfter years in the 12-step programme of Alcoholics Anonymous, James becomes a sponsor to newcomer Luka. The pair bond over black coffee, trade stories and build a fragile friendship out of their shared experiences. But as Luka approaches step five – the moment of confession – dangerous truths emerge, threatening the trust on which both of their recoveries depend. \\n \\nFinn den Hertog directs the provocative and entertaining production filmed live from @sohoplace on London’s West End.\",\"starring\":\"Jack Lowden, Martin Freeman\",\"directedBy\":\"Finn den Hertog\",\"producedBy\":null,\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":100,\"genre\":null,\"allGenres\":\"\",\"rating\":\"TBC\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"WLV4Ho-eCTo\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-11-27\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-11-18\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"475713\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"Lrc Fifth Step - NT Live 2025 (Theatre), The [Unknown]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"411\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"362926\",\"time\":\"2025-11-18T20:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":14,\"screenId\":\"442\",\"seatsRemaining\":46,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"362927\",\"time\":\"2025-11-27T19:30:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":83,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":18,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"362928\",\"time\":\"2025-12-01T14:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":41,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":60,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"362929\",\"time\":\"2025-12-09T20:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":29,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":72,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"31219\",\"name\":\"Children of Men\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"children-of-men\",\"posterImage\":\"781rnopo4isfz9pd0xgv19iibq2z\",\"bannerImage\":\"kvinehcv6qxc83iee3c9jf4csxrk\",\"synopsis\":\"In 2027, in a chaotic world in which humans can no longer procreate, a former activist agrees to help transport a miraculously pregnant woman to a sanctuary at sea, where her child’s birth may help scientists save the future of humankind (taken from Letterboxd)\\n\\nJoin us by first reading P. D. James’s classic dystopian novel of the same name, and then attending the screening of Cuarón’s iconic adaptation on 19th November. Afterwards there will be a guided discussion, followed by the opportunity to mingle with your fellow biblio- and cinephiles.\",\"starring\":\"Julianne Moore, Chiwetel Ejiofor, Michael Caine, Clive Owen, Charlie Hunnam\",\"directedBy\":\"Alfonso Cuaron\",\"producedBy\":null,\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":107,\"genre\":\"Drama\",\"allGenres\":null,\"rating\":\"15\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2VT2apoX90o\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-11-19\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-11-19\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"23923\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"Children Of Men, The (2D) [15]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"419\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"362968\",\"time\":\"2025-11-19T19:30:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":19,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":82,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser ad-free books-on-film\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"31226\",\"name\":\"Out of the Past\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"out-of-the-past\",\"posterImage\":\"ir2na9xeg62hznuyv2mrv8fa4ei5\",\"bannerImage\":\"ztewnl3b2gcsmabtz22irzh6d0vj\",\"synopsis\":\"About the film:\\nRobert Mitchum and Jane Greer co-star in this noir classic from director Jacques Tourneur, based on the 1946 novel Build My Gallows High (the film’s title in the UK), by Daniel Mainwaring. Mitchum stars as retired private eye Jeff Bailey, who’s dragged back into a world of sex, corruption, danger and double crosses, all centred around crime boss Kirk Douglas and his duplicitous girlfriend Kathie Moffat (Greer), one of film noir’s quintessential femme fatales.\\n\\nAbout Noirvember:\\nLocal film critic and podcaster Matthew Turner returns for a second mini season of film noir classics, which will run exclusively at Chiswick Cinema throughout November 2025.\\n\\nBroadly speaking, the term film noir (coined by French film critics) refers to Hollywood thrillers and dramas from the 1940s and ’50s that were perceived to have a degree of darkness and cynicism, reflecting post-WII attitudes at the time. Film noir stories frequently revolve around crime, corruption, greed, illicit sex and murder, exposing the dark heart beating beneath the American Dream.\\n\\nJoin us for five film noir classics, all of which showcase key elements of the genre, from hard-boiled dialogue (derived from the detective novels that were often adapted into thrillers), voiceover narration and shadowy lighting to femme fatales, murder plots and decidely unhappy endings.\\n\\nLike last year, each film will be introduced by Matthew Turner, a lifelong film noir enthusiast, who will also be around in the bar after each screening. In addition, audiences are invited to post about the films online, using the hashtag #Noirvember, a great source of other film noir recommendations.\",\"starring\":\"Robert Mitchum, Kirk Douglas, Jane Greer\",\"directedBy\":\"Jacques Tourneur\",\"producedBy\":null,\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":97,\"genre\":null,\"allGenres\":null,\"rating\":\"PG\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bMgGuCIZnsM\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-11-19\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-11-19\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"929301\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"Out Of The Past (Re: 1998) (2D) [PG]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"419\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"363028\",\"time\":\"2025-11-19T19:45:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":23,\"screenId\":\"441\",\"seatsRemaining\":78,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser intro\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"29165\",\"name\":\"National Theatre Live: Mrs. Warren’s Profession\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"national-theatre-live-mrs-warrens-profession\",\"posterImage\":\"bqwc5whic9jz8t1cnyooqv2emths\",\"bannerImage\":\"5omro1djaobalm3qvp2k7yf0lsv7\",\"synopsis\":\"Five-time Olivier Award winner Imelda Staunton (The Crown) joins forces with her real-life daughter Bessie Carter (Bridgerton) for the very first time,\\nplaying mother and daughter in Bernard Shaw’s incendiary moral classic.\\nVivie Warren is a woman ahead of her time. Her mother, however, is a product of that old patriarchal order.\\nExploiting it has earned Mrs. Warren a fortune – but at what cost?\\nFilmed live from the West End, this new production reunites Staunton with director Dominic Cooke (Follies, Good), exploring the clash between morality and independence, traditions and progress.\",\"starring\":\"Imelda Staunton, Bessie Carter\",\"directedBy\":\"Dominic Cooke\",\"producedBy\":null,\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":117,\"genre\":null,\"allGenres\":null,\"rating\":\"12A\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"FhGE6dW7He4\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-10-23\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-11-20\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"475712\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"Lrc Mrs. Warren's Profession - NT Live 2025 (Theatre) [Unknown]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"411\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"362938\",\"time\":\"2025-11-20T19:30:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":30,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":71,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"31256\",\"name\":\"Wicked Double Bill\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"wicked-double-bill\",\"posterImage\":\"8vvu03rftoi9aaqnkx1q0iu7xjbn\",\"bannerImage\":\"zqsey2jlc00ujy33m1r1d1q4jtnv\",\"synopsis\":\"See the new Wicked in a double bill with part one. There is a 20 minute interval between screenings.\",\"starring\":\"Cynthia Erivo, Ariana Grande, Jonathan Bailey\",\"directedBy\":\"Jon M. Chu\",\"producedBy\":\"David Stone, Marc Platt\",\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":319,\"genre\":\"Drama\",\"allGenres\":\"Drama, Fantasy, Romance\",\"rating\":\"TBC\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"a1l5pm5YHQ8\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-11-21\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-11-20\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":29.6923,\"tmdbId\":\"967941\",\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"259372\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"Extremely Wicked, Shockingly Evil And Vile (2D) [15]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"410\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"363350\",\"time\":\"2025-11-20T17:30:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":0,\"screenId\":\"439\",\"seatsRemaining\":125,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"29188\",\"name\":\"Wicked: For Good\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"wicked-for-good\",\"posterImage\":\"8vvu03rftoi9aaqnkx1q0iu7xjbn\",\"bannerImage\":\"zqsey2jlc00ujy33m1r1d1q4jtnv\",\"synopsis\":\"And now whatever way our stories end, I know you have rewritten mine by being my friend …\\n\\nLast year’s global cinematic cultural sensation, which became the most successful Broadway film adaptation of all time, now reaches its epic, electrifying, emotional conclusion in Wicked: For Good. \\n\\nDirected once again by award-winning director Jon M. Chu and starring the spectacular returning cast, led by Academy Award® nominated superstars Cynthia Erivo and Ariana Grande, the final chapter of the untold story of the witches of Oz begins with Elphaba and Glinda estranged and living with the consequences of their choices. \\n\\nElphaba (Cynthia Erivo), now demonised as The Wicked Witch of the West, lives in exile, hidden within the Ozian forest while continuing her fight for the freedom of Oz’s silenced Animals and desperately trying to expose the truth she knows about The Wizard (Jeff Goldblum).  \\n\\nGlinda, meanwhile, has become the glamorous symbol of Goodness for all of Oz, living at the palace in Emerald City and revelling in the perks of fame and popularity. Under the instruction of Madame Morrible (Oscar® winner Michelle Yeoh), Glinda is deployed to serve as an effervescent comfort to Oz, reassuring the masses that all is well under the rule of The Wizard.  \\n\\nAs Glinda’s stardom expands and she prepares to marry Prince Fiyero (Olivier award winner and Emmy and SAG nominee Jonathan Bailey) in a spectacular Ozian wedding, she is haunted by her separation from Elphaba. She attempts to broker a conciliation between Elphaba and The Wizard, but those efforts will fail, driving Elphaba and Glinda only further apart. The aftershocks will transform Boq (Tony nominee Ethan Slater) and Fiyero forever, and threaten the safety of Elphaba’s sister, Nessarose (Marissa Bode), when a girl from Kansas comes crashing into all their lives. \\n\\nAs an angry mob rises against the Wicked Witch, Glinda and Elphaba will need to come together one final time. With their singular friendship now the fulcrum of their futures, they will need to truly see each other, with honesty and empathy, if they are to change themselves, and all of Oz, for good.\",\"starring\":\"Cynthia Erivo, Ariana Grande, Jonathan Bailey\",\"directedBy\":\"Jon M. Chu\",\"producedBy\":\"David Stone, Marc Platt\",\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":137,\"genre\":\"Drama\",\"allGenres\":\"Drama, Fantasy, Romance\",\"rating\":\"PG\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"a1l5pm5YHQ8\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-11-21\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2025-11-21\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":29.6923,\"tmdbId\":\"967941\",\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"361220\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"WICKED: FOR GOOD [Unknown]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"410\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"362773\",\"time\":\"2025-11-21T11:30:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":0,\"screenId\":\"439\",\"seatsRemaining\":125,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser\\\"}\"},